{"title":"Common sense in charge","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/968181716/0/marginalrevolution~Common-sense-in-charge.html","date":1787593163000,"content":"<blockquote><p>…children are increasingly seen as interfering with the freedom of parents; views on whether mothers of young children should work have become markedly more progressive and account for a substantially larger share of the decline among the tertiary-educated; and fewer people believe that women or men need children to lead a fulfilled life. This last attitude changed most over the decade and is the largest contributor to the fall in intended fertility, above all among less-educated women.</p></blockquote>\r\n<p>That is from <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.nber.org/papers/w35651#fromrss\" target=\"_blank\">a new NBER working paper</a> by <span> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.nber.org/people/raquel_fernandez\">Raquel Fernández, </a></span><span><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.nber.org/people/ines_berniell\">Inés Berniell, and </a></span><span><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.nber.org/people/milagros_onofri\">Milagros Onofri.</a> </span></p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/08/common-sense-in-charge.html\">Common sense in charge</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/968181716/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/28/968181716/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/fblike20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/29/968181716/marginalrevolution,\"><i